  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving understanding and respect for human rights and civic responsibilities amongst Burundian po</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to contribute to improving peaceful cohabitation in 4 municipalities of Bujumbura diocese through
trainings, sensitization and advocacy for respect of Human Rights. On one hand the project seeks to increase knowledge and promote consideration for Human Rights by Police Forces, and on the other to increase Communities (Particularly
taxi drivers providing trans border services and traders) understanding of their rights and civic responsibilities. 
This project will use a bottom &#x2013; up approach, by strengthening existing networks of &#x201c;Peace Apostles&#x201d; (Apotres de Paix) in selected Basic Ecclesiastic Community (CEB: Communaute Ecclesiastique de Base) in Kamenge, Cibitoke, Musaga and Kanyosha.
CDJP Bujumbura will lead and coordinate an exchange forum between Peace Apostles and Local administrative and police authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
